{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ruzm1kHq1Fst39AX2Kfa8s","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Supabase docs Row Level Security\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Securing your API\",\"url\":\"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/api/securing-your-api\"},{\"title\":\"Securing your data\",\"url\":\"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/secure-data\"},{\"title\":\"Database\",\"url\":\"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/overview\"},{\"title\":\"RAG with Permissions\",\"url\":\"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/ai/rag-with-permissions\"},{\"title\":\"Tables and data\",\"url\":\"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/tables\"},{\"title\":\"API keys\",\"url\":\"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/getting-started/api-keys\"},{\"title\":\"Auth\",\"url\":\"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/auth\"},{\"title\":\"Production Checklist\",\"url\":\"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/deployment/going-into-prod\"},{\"title\":\"Supabase Docs\",\"url\":\"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/troubleshooting/storage-error-403-forbidden-new-row-violates-row-level-security-policy-on-upload-a94384\"},{\"title\":\"Realtime Authorization\",\"url\":\"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/realtime/authorization\"}]\n\nThe search returned a useful set of Supabase docs on Row Level Security (RLS). The main pages are the Securing your API guide, the Tables and data guide, the API keys page, and the Production Checklist.\n\n- **Grants and RLS are separate layers.** The API guide describes two controls: grants decide which roles can reach an object, and RLS policies decide which rows those roles can touch. Use both controls for every exposed object.\n- **No policy means no rows.** The Tables and data guide says that a table with RLS enabled but no policy returns nothing through the Data API. It also notes that the table owner and roles with BYPASSRLS are not subject to policies.\n- **Enable RLS on every exposed table.** The Production Checklist recommends turning it on for all tables from the Dashboard.\n- **Keys and bypassing.** The API keys page explains that publishable keys map to the `anon` or `authenticated` roles, which RLS policies match on. Secret keys map to `service_role`, which bypasses RLS, so they should stay on the server.\n- **User-scoped access.** The Auth docs say the user's auth token scopes row access when used together with RLS policies.\n- **Other uses.** Realtime Authorization uses RLS policies on the `realtime.messages` table to control channel access, and the RAG guide shows RLS being used with pgvector to restrict search results.\n\nEach of these points comes from a single search result, so the summary is not a full read of any page. The \"Securing your data\" page is also a useful starting point.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1fafd49c-c7a3-458c-9921-4e6ed3d183f4","uuid":"9b92d3bc-d422-4cfc-bc06-32cab023d696","timestamp":"2026-10-16T23:13:01.909Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Supabase docs Row Level Security","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_011D3XLEAoTjao6BVTAq3XMQ","content":[{"title":"Securing your API","url":"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/api/securing-your-api"},{"title":"Securing your data","url":"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/secure-data"},{"title":"Database","url":"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/overview"},{"title":"RAG with Permissions","url":"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/ai/rag-with-permissions"},{"title":"Tables and data","url":"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/tables"},{"title":"API keys","url":"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/getting-started/api-keys"},{"title":"Auth","url":"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/auth"},{"title":"Production Checklist","url":"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/deployment/going-into-prod"},{"title":"Supabase Docs","url":"https://supabase.com/docs/guides/troubleshooting/storage-error-403-